# Page debug flags

## Debug button

- Every page that needs dev-only controls gets a **Debug** button (bottom-right), same pattern as Search / Library (`fixed bottom-4 right-4`, slide-over panel, `BugIcon`).
- The panel and its toggles render **only when `import.meta.env.DEV`**. Production always uses the current shipped defaults.
- Keep flags compact (small segmented toggles). Put hints in `title` tooltips, not large cards.
- Colocate page flags in that page’s debug panel (or a `*DebugPanel` component used only there). Do not dump unrelated flags into other pages.

## Debug design pages (DEV only)

- Temp design / comparison routes are listed in `app/lib/debug-pages.ts` and rendered by `DebugPagesNav` (root): **bottom-right, stacked above the Debug button**, **only when `import.meta.env.DEV`**.
- When creating a new temp page: add `{ path, label }` to `DEBUG_PAGES`.
- When deleting a temp page after a winner: remove it from `DEBUG_PAGES` as well as the route.

## When changing UI

When asked to change UI (layout, chrome, colors, components, etc.):

1. **Default: preserve the current UI** behind a **dev-only feature flag** in **that page’s** Debug panel.
2. Ship the new UI as the default; the flag switches back to the previous version for comparison.
3. Name flags clearly (e.g. Card: Glass / Legacy, Progress: Cover / Original).
4. Wire production paths so they **always** take the new default — never the legacy branch — unless `import.meta.env.DEV` and the flag says otherwise.

## Opt out of preserving

If the user says **not** to save / keep / preserve the current UI (e.g. “don’t keep the old one”, “no feature flag”, “replace it”):

- **Do not** add a legacy/flag path.
- **Notify the user** in the reply that the previous UI was discarded and is not recoverable via Debug.

## Do not

- Leave temp design-comparison routes around after a winner is chosen (see apple-glass design exploration rule).
- Expose these UI rollback flags outside DEV.
